> associator i, j, k
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -1 - (-1) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> associator 1+i, 1+j, 1+k
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = 2i + 2k - (2i + 2k) = 0
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> commutator i, j
[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k
  they do not commute
> conj(1+i)
conj((1+i)) = 1 - i
  check: equal numerically (1 - 1i, complex arithmetic)
> abs(1+2i+3j+4k)
  note: i, j, k are the quaternion units: i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1, ij = k = -ji (say k: real for a variable k)
sqrt(30)
> 1e3
1000
> 2.0e1
20
> table quaternion
multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:
      |   1   i   j   k
  ----+----------------
    1 |   1   i   j   k
    i |   i  -1   k  -j
    j |   j  -k  -1   i
    k |   k   j  -i  -1
  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign
> zerodivisors cd 8
the octonions have no zero divisors: |ab| = |a||b|, so ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0
